Looting the application

The app lived in /opt/app. Reviewing the source confirmed both vulnerabilities and revealed a backup/ and db/ directory:

bash
cat /opt/app/app.js
SQLi: `SELECT * FROM users WHERE username = '${username}' AND password = '${password}'` — raw string concatenation, confirming the admin' OR 1=1 -- - bypass.
RCE: the /preview/:filename route calls require(filePath) on .js files, executing them — the exact vector used by rev.js.

The real prizes were the backup and database files:

bash
cat /opt/app/backup/shadow.bak
